 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 508223,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Graph the equation <span data-math=\"y = 3x - 1\">y = 3x - 1</span> by plotting points.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"y = 3x - 1\"></span></p>\n<p>Find three points that are solutions to the equation. Choose three values for <i>x</i>.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><i>x</i></td>\n<td><i>y</i></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>–1</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Substitute into the equation to find the values for <i>y</i>.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><i>x</i></td>\n<td><i>y</i></td>\n<td><span data-math=\"y=3x–1\"></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>–1</td>\n<td>–4</td>\n<td><span data-math=\"3(–1) – 1 = –3 – 1 = –4\"></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>–1</td>\n<td><span data-math=\"3(0) – 1 = 0 – 1 = –1\"></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td><span data-math=\"3(1) – 1 = 3 – 1 = 2\"></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Plot the points. Check that they line up and draw the line.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<img src=\"https://exercises.openstax.org/rails/active_storage/blobs/proxy/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsibWVzc2FnZSI6IkJBaHBBbUVNIiwiZXhwIjpudWxsLCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--1535ff2b5c886f7ae775ffd1b6cb204fb40f7bdf/CS_Figure_05_05_012.jpg\" alt=\"A line is plotted on an x y coordinate plane. The x and y axes range from negative 12 to 12, in increments of 2. The line passes through the following points, (negative 2, negative 7), (0, negative 1), (2, 5), and (4, 11). Note: all values are approximate.\">"
    }
   ],
